      "notes": "One logical LNC2 unit combines two physical NC-v3 Tensor Engines: dense BF16/FP16 peak = 2 x 79 = 158 TFLOPS (https://awsdocs-neuron.readthedocs-hosted.com/en/v2.27.0/about-neuron/arch/neuron-hardware/neuron-core-v3.html). HBM bandwidth 725 GB/s is a nominal equal-bank analysis estimate: published chip 2.9 TB/s divided among four 24GB banks, each shared by one core pair; AWS does not independently publish or guarantee this unit rate (https://awsdocs-neuron.readthedocs-hosted.com/en/v2.27.0/about-neuron/arch/neuron-features/logical-neuroncore-config.html and https://awsdocs-neuron.readthedocs-hosted.com/en/v2.27.0/about-neuron/arch/neuron-hardware/trainium2.html). Roofline/R6/R7 results depend on that bandwidth assumption; it is not measured timing. Physical-core intervals are unioned per invocation. Capacity comes from neuron-ls; price and whole-chip heterogeneous compute peaks are not assigned to this unit."
